	doi = {10.13360/j.issn.2096-1359.202008018},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85113671652&doi=10.13360%2fj.issn.2096-1359.202008018&partnerID=40&md5=076ac8219410970e58152b43ad6d4755},
	abstract = {The individual tree position extraction in an artificial forest area refers to mark each tree in the artificial forest area on a map, allowing forestry managers to make statistics, query and follow-up applications of the forest. Accurate extraction of the individual tree position helps evaluate tree yields in forest areas, monitoring changes in the number of trees in forest areas, etc. At the same time, it is also a prerequisite for the extraction of the individual tree crown, cal culation of forest canopy density, vegetation health monitoring and forest pest monitoring. When extracting the indi vidual tree position from UAV RGB images, due to the color similarity between tree crown and grass, shrub and other non-tree crown vegetations, and the adhesion between tree crowns, the accuracy of individual tree position extraction is not high. In order to solve these problems, an individual tree position extraction method based on the canopy height model (CHM) and the morphological thinning algorithm was proposed in this study. Firstly, according to the UAV RGB images, the digital orthophoto map (DOM) , the digital elevation model (DHM) and the digital surface model (DSM) were generated. The visible band difference vegetation index ( VDVI) was used to separate the vegetation from the non-vegetation. Secondly, the CHM of the artificial forest area was constructed using DSM and DHM, which can separate the tree crown from the non-tree crown vegetation in terms of elevation difference. Finally, in order to improve the accuracy of individual tree position extraction, the morphological thinning algorithm was used to remove the adhesion between tree crowns. According to the above method, the position of individual tree was extracted and the accuracy was verified. Taking an artificial forest area in Chenggong campus of Kunming University of Science and Technology in Yunnan Province as the experimental forest area, the proposed method was directly based on VDVI vegetation images, being used to extract the location of individual tree in the artificial forest area. The accuracy of in- dividual tree extracted by the proposed method was 91.67%, the missing extraction rate was 8.33%, and the error ex traction rate was 0.24%; while the accuracy of individual tree extracted directly based on VDVI vegetation image was 88.05%.the missing extraction rate was 11.95%, and the error extraction rate was 21.58%. The experimental results showed that the proposed method has higher accuracy for extracting individual trees from the artificial forest area. © 2021 Nanjing Forestry University. All rights reserved},
	author_keywords = {Artificial forest area; Individual tree position; Rgb image; Uav; Vdvi},
	type = {Article},
	publication_stage = {Final},
