	keywords = {Adolescent; Adolescent Behavior; Arsenic; Bangladesh; Cohort Studies; Environmental Exposure; Female; Humans; Longitudinal Studies; Male; Nervous System Diseases; Pilot Projects; Thyroid Hormones; Water Pollutants, Chemical; Bangladesh; Aquifers; Association reactions; Biomarkers; Body fluids; Groundwater pollution; Groundwater resources; Hormones; Hydrogeology; Potable water; arsenic; liothyronine; thyroid peroxidase antibody; thyrotropin; thyroxine; arsenic; thyroid hormone; Alluvial aquifers; Arsenic exposure; Bengal delta plains; Geogenic arsenics; Longitudinal study; Neurotoxicity; Possible mechanisms; Thyroid hormones; aquifer; arsenic; biomarker; drinking water; health impact; hormone; performance assessment; pollution exposure; young population; adolescent; adult; aged; aquifer; Article; Bangladesh; cognition; cohort analysis; correlational study; cross-sectional study; female; Holocene; human; liothyronine blood level; long term exposure; longitudinal study; male; neurotoxicity; pilot study; priority journal; protein blood level; simple reaction time; thyroid hormone blood level; thyrotropin blood level; thyroxine blood level; water contamination; adolescent behavior; blood; chemically induced; drug effect; environmental exposure; neurologic disease; pathophysiology; water pollutant; Arsenic},
