	abstract = {In this study, a novel setup was developed to measure the vertical profile of particle number size distribution (PNSD) and meteorological parameters by using hexacopter equipped with a portable instrument package including a custom-built scanning mobility particle sizer, an optical particle counter and temperature and relative humidity (RH) sensors. By using this setup, a field experiment was carried out to investigate the vertical profiles of RH, temperature, PNSD ranged from 8 to 245 nm, and particle number concentration with the diameter ranges of 0.3–0.5 μm and 0.5–1.0 μm from the ground up to 300 m above ground level in a rural site of the North China Plain. New particle formation (NPF) event in a vertical scale was observed during the daytime cruises. The newly formed particles showed a heterogeneous vertical distribution, indicating the inhomogeneous occurrence of the NPF event vertically. During the daytime, the vertical variations in number concentration of particles larger than 0.3 μm was not obvious, while, showed a tendency to decrease associated with the increasing altitude in the evening. The newly-developed unmanned aerial vehicle research platform could be applied to study the vertical NPF events and transport processes of air pollutants within the atmospheric boundary layer and urban canopy, and to monitor source emissions with the purpose of environment management. © 2019 Elsevier B.V.},
	author_keywords = {Air pollution; Hexacopter; Particle number size distribution; Unmanned aerial vehicle},
	keywords = {China; North China Plain; Air pollution; Antennas; Atmospheric boundary layer; Atmospheric humidity; Atmospheric temperature; Boundary layer flow; Size distribution; Unmanned aerial vehicles (UAV); Urban transportation; Environment management; Hexacopter; Meteorological parameters; Optical particle counters; Particle number concentration; Particle number size distribution; Scanning mobility particle sizer; Temperature and relative humidity; aerosol; air temperature; atmospheric pollution; relative humidity; size distribution; unmanned vehicle; vertical distribution; air pollutant; air pollution; airflow; altitude; Article; atmosphere; canopy; China; circadian rhythm; controlled study; environmental aspects and related phenomena; environmental management; environmental monitoring; environmental parameters; environmental temperature; geographic and geological phenomena; geographic distribution; hexacopter; humidity; meteorology; particle number size distribution; particle size; plain; pollution and pollution related phenomena; pollution transport; priority journal; rural area; sampling; urban area; Atmospheric aerosols},
	type = {Article},
